BrosCommunityEditionFiles/bgm.bnk filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.bnk filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# Binary game files: never touch line endings
*.fsv    binary
*.tcmbpkg binary
*.tadjpkg binary
*.tbl    binary
*.vfxb   binary

# Text files — store as LF
*.py     text eol=lf
*.csv    text eol=lf
*.json   text eol=lf
*.txt    text eol=lf
*.bat    text eol=crlf

*.dll binary

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Game payload is bytes, not text
#
# Anything a version copies into the game folder must reach it exactly as Steam
# shipped it. Measured 2026-09-21 against a clean install of build 21095206:
# the "*.csv text eol=lf" rule above had stripped the CRLF from every
# Script/ObjectConfig/*.csv, and each launch injected the stripped copies into
# the game. None of them was intentionally modified. The original bytes are not
# recoverable from history; they were restored from the clean install.
#
# -text disables end-of-line conversion while still allowing a textual diff.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
GameVersions/**/Script/**    -text
GameVersions/**/Motion/**    -text
GameVersions/**/00HIGH/**    -text
GameVersions/**/01MIDDLE/**  -text
GameVersions/**/02LOW/**     -text
GameVersions/**/Demo/**      -text
GameVersions/**/Overlay/**   -text
GameModes/**/Script/**       -text
GameModes/**/Motion/**       -text
Reworks/**/Script/**         -text
Reworks/**/Motion/**         -text
Files/Stock/**               -text
